We use induction to construct all desired paths $P_1,\dots,P_k$ with desired lengths $n_1,\dots,n_k$. Without loss of generality, assume $n_1 \leq \dots \leq n_k$.

For the base case, let $i=1$. %Assume first that $x_1\notin Q'$. 
