The proposed planted-path family clears G and V but fails H:

- Track A: the paper proves existence, not hardness for a generated distribution. A dense-graph path heuristic solved 8/8 tested instances at \(n=256\).
- Track B: the mechanical and compact routes both require 253 vertex extensions, so there is no compression or insight gap.
- Median solving time was 0.267545 seconds.
- This is not `cap_bound`; increasing \(n\) only adds routine polynomial work and answer length.

Full theorem audit, measurements, and rejection rationale are in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1408.0408/REJECTED.md). The source definition is Theorem 2 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1408.0408).
